Article 33 The types of principal punishments are as follows:
(1) public surveillance;
(2) criminal detention;
(3) fixed-term imprisonment;
(4) life imprisonment;
(5) the death penalty.

Article 34 The types of supplementary punishments are as follows:
(1) a fine;
(2) deprivation of political rights;
(3) confiscation of property.
Supplementary punishments may also be imposed independently.

Article 39 A criminal offender sentenced to public surveillance shall, during the execution period, comply with the following provisions:
(1) observe laws and administrative regulations, and submit to supervision;
(2) without the approval of the executing authority, shall not exercise the rights to freedom of speech, press, assembly, association, procession, or demonstration;
(3) report his or her activities in accordance with the regulations of the executing authority;
(4) observe the regulations of the executing authority concerning meeting visitors;
(5) report to the executing authority for approval when leaving the city or county where he or she resides or moving to another residence.
For criminal offenders sentenced to public surveillance, they shall receive equal pay for equal work in labor.

Article 54: Deprivation of political rights means depriving the following rights:
(1) The right to vote and the right to be elected;
(2) The rights to freedom of speech, press, assembly, association, procession, and demonstration;
(3) The right to hold a position in a state organ;
(4) The right to hold a leading position in a state-owned company, enterprise, institution, or people's organization.

Article 72: For a criminal sentenced to criminal detention or fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, if the following conditions are met concurrently, probation may be declared; for a person under the age of 18, a pregnant woman, or a person who has reached the age of 75 among them, probation shall be declared:
(1) The circumstances of the crime are minor;
(2) There is a showing of repentance;
(3) There is no danger of committing another crime;
(4) The declaration of probation does not have a major adverse impact on the community where the person resides.
When declaring probation, the criminal may, based on the circumstances of the crime, be concurrently prohibited from engaging in specific activities, entering specific areas or places, or contacting specific persons during the probation period.
If a criminal placed on probation is also sentenced to supplementary punishment, the supplementary punishment shall still be executed.

Article 75: A criminal placed on probation shall observe the following provisions:
(1) Observe laws and administrative regulations, and submit to supervision;
(2) Report his or her activities in accordance with the provisions of the supervisory authority;
(3) Observe the provisions of the supervisory authority regarding receiving visitors;
(4) Report to and obtain approval from the supervisory authority before leaving the city or county of residence or changing residence.

Article 78: For a criminal sentenced to public surveillance, criminal detention, fixed-term imprisonment, or life imprisonment, during the execution period, if he or she earnestly observes the prison regulations, accepts education and reform, and shows genuine repentance, or if he or she performs meritorious service, the punishment may be commuted; if any of the following major meritorious service is performed, the punishment shall be commuted:
(1) Preventing another person from committing a major criminal activity;
(2) Reporting major criminal activities inside or outside prison, which is verified as true;
(3) Making an invention or significant technical innovation;
(4) Sacrificing oneself to save others in daily production or life;
(5) Making outstanding contributions in resisting natural disasters or eliminating major accidents;
(6) Making other major contributions to the state and society.
The actual term of execution after commutation shall not be less than the following periods:
(1) For those sentenced to public surveillance, criminal detention, or fixed-term imprisonment, not less than one-half of the original sentence;
(2) For those sentenced to life imprisonment, not less than 13 years;
(3) For criminals sentenced to death with a reprieve for whom the People's Court, in accordance with the provisions of paragraph 2 of Article 50 of this Law, restricts commutation, after the reprieve period expires and it is commuted to life imprisonment according to law, not less than 25 years; after the reprieve period expires and it is commuted to 25 years of fixed-term imprisonment according to law, not less than 20 years.

Article 84 A criminal who is granted parole shall observe the following provisions:
(1) Observe laws and administrative regulations, and submit to supervision;
(2) Report his or her activities in accordance with the regulations of the supervisory authority;
(3) Observe the regulations of the supervisory authority concerning meeting visitors; and
(4) Obtain approval from the supervisory authority before leaving the city or county where he or she resides or moving to another place.

Article 87 A crime shall no longer be prosecuted after the following periods:
(1) Five years, if the maximum statutory punishment is fixed-term imprisonment of less than five years;
(2) Ten years, if the maximum statutory punishment is fixed-term imprisonment of five years or more but less than ten years;
(3) Fifteen years, if the maximum statutory punishment is fixed-term imprisonment of ten years or more; and
(4) Twenty years, if the maximum statutory punishment is life imprisonment or death penalty. If prosecution is deemed necessary after twenty years, it must be submitted to the Supreme People's Procuratorate for approval.

Article 91 For the purposes of this Law, "public property" means the following property:
(1) State-owned property;
(2) Property collectively owned by the working masses;
(3) Property donated for poverty alleviation and other public welfare undertakings or special fund property.
Private property under the management, use, or transportation of state organs, state-owned companies, enterprises, collective enterprises, or people's organizations shall be treated as public property.

Article 92 For the purposes of this Law, "property privately owned by citizens" means the following property:
(1) Citizens' lawful income, savings, housing, and other means of livelihood;
(2) Means of production owned by individuals or families according to law;
(3) Lawful property of individual businesses and private enterprises; and
(4) Shares, stocks, bonds, and other property owned by individuals according to law.

Article 142: Whoever produces or sells substandard drugs, causing serious harm to human health, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined; if the consequences are especially serious, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years or life imprisonment, and a fine shall also be imposed or property shall be confiscated.
Where a person in a drug-use entity, knowing a drug to be substandard, provides it to another for use, the penalty shall be imposed in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.
Article 142-1: Whoever, in violation of drug administration laws and regulations, falls under any of the following circumstances, if it is sufficient to seriously endanger human health, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention, and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if it causes serious harm to human health or there are other serious circumstances, the sentence shall be fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years, and a fine shall also be imposed:
(1) producing or selling drugs prohibited by the drug regulatory department of the State Council;
(2) producing or importing drugs without obtaining relevant drug approval certificates or documents, or selling the aforesaid drugs with knowledge thereof;
(3) providing false certificates, data, materials, samples or adopting other fraudulent means in drug application for registration;
(4) fabricating production or inspection records.
Where a person engages in the conduct in the preceding paragraph which also constitutes a crime under Article 141 or 142 of this Law or any other crime, he shall be convicted and punished in accordance with the provisions on the heavier punishment.

Article 154: Where the following smuggling acts constitute a crime under the provisions of this Section, the offender shall be convicted and punished in accordance with the provisions of Article 153 of this Law:
(1) without permission from the Customs and without making up the amount of taxes payable, selling for profit within the territory of the People's Republic of China authorized imported bonded goods such as raw materials, parts, finished products, and equipment for processing with supplied materials, assembling with supplied parts, or compensation trade;
(2) without permission from the Customs and without making up the amount of taxes payable, selling for profit within the territory of the People's Republic of China goods or articles imported with specific tax reduction or exemption.

Article 155: The following acts shall be considered as crimes of smuggling and punished in accordance with the relevant provisions of this Section:
(1) directly and illegally purchasing from smugglers articles that are prohibited by the State from being imported, or directly and illegally purchasing from smugglers other goods or articles that are smuggled in, if the amount involved is relatively large;
(2) transporting, purchasing, or selling within the internal waters, territorial seas, boundary rivers, or boundary lakes articles that are prohibited by the State from being imported or exported, or transporting, purchasing, or selling within these areas goods or articles whose import or export is restricted by the State, if the amount involved is relatively large and there are no lawful certificates.

Article 169 Where a directly responsible person in charge of a state-owned company or enterprise or its superior competent department, by engaging in malpractices for personal gain, converts state-owned assets into shares at a low price or sells them at a low price, thereby causing significant losses to state interests, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention; if they cause particularly significant losses to state interests, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years.

Article 169-1 Where a director, supervisor, or senior officer of a listed company, in violation of their duty of loyalty to the company and by taking advantage of their position, manipulates the listed company to commit any of the following acts, thereby causing significant losses to the interests of the listed company, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention, and shall also or solely be fined; if they cause particularly significant losses to the interests of the listed company, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years, and shall also be fined:

(1) providing funds, commodities, services, or other assets to other units or individuals without consideration;
(2) providing or accepting funds, commodities, services, or other assets on obviously unfair terms;
(3) providing funds, commodities, services, or other assets to units or individuals that obviously do not have the ability to repay;
(4) providing guarantees for units or individuals that obviously do not have the ability to repay, or providing guarantees for other units or individuals without justifiable reasons;
(5) waiving claims or assuming debts without justifiable reasons; or
(6) using other methods to harm the interests of the listed company.

Where the controlling shareholder or actual controller of a listed company instigates the directors, supervisors, or senior officers of the listed company to commit any of the acts specified in the preceding paragraph, they shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.

Where the controlling shareholder or actual controller of a listed company who commits the crime specified in the preceding paragraph is a unit, the unit shall be fined, and the directly responsible person in charge and other directly liable persons shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the first paragraph.

Article 177 Whoever forges or alters financial instruments under any of the following circumstances shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also or solely be fined not less than RMB 20,000 but not more than RMB 200,000; if the circumstances are serious, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined not less than RMB 50,000 but not more than RMB 500,000; if the circumstances are particularly serious, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years or life imprisonment, and shall also be fined not less than RMB 50,000 but not more than RMB 500,000 or have property confiscated:

(1) forging or altering bills of exchange, promissory notes, or cheques;
(2) forging or altering other bank settlement vouchers such as entrusted collection vouchers, remittance vouchers, or bank deposit certificates;
(3) forging or altering letters of credit or accompanying documents or instruments; or
(4) forging credit cards.

Where a unit commits the crime specified in the preceding paragraph, the unit shall be fined, and the directly responsible person in charge and other directly liable persons shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.

Article 177-1 Whoever hinders credit card management under any of the following circumstances shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention, and shall also or solely be fined not less than RMB 10,000 but not more than RMB 100,000; if the quantity is huge or if other serious circumstances exist, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined not less than RMB 20,000 but not more than RMB 200,000:

(1) holding or transporting counterfeit credit cards knowing them to be counterfeit, or holding or transporting counterfeit blank credit cards knowing them to be counterfeit, in relatively large quantities;
(2) illegally holding credit cards belonging to another person in relatively large quantities;
(3) obtaining credit cards by using false identity certificates to defraud them; or
(4) selling, purchasing, or providing credit cards that are counterfeited or obtained by using false identity certificates, for another person.

Whoever steals, purchases, or illegally provides the information data of credit cards belonging to another person shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.

Where an employee of a bank or other financial institution, by taking advantage of their position, commits the crime specified in the second paragraph, they shall be given a severe punishment.

Article 182 Whoever, under any of the following circumstances, manipulates the securities or futures market to affect the price or volume of securities or futures trading, and the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if the circumstances are especially serious, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined:
(1) acting alone or in collusion, concentrating capital, shareholding, or position advantages, or utilizing information advantages, to jointly or continuously trade in securities or futures;
(2) colluding with another person to engage in mutual securities or futures transactions at a prearranged time, price, and manner;
(3) conducting securities transactions between accounts actually controlled by oneself, or selling and buying futures contracts with oneself as the counterparty;
(4) frequently or substantially entering purchase or sale orders for securities or futures contracts without the intention of completing the transaction, and subsequently canceling such orders;
(5) inducing investors to trade in securities or futures by using false or uncertain material information;
(6) making public evaluations, forecasts, or investment recommendations regarding securities, securities issuers, or futures trading targets, while simultaneously engaging in reverse securities trading or related futures trading; or
(7) manipulating the securities or futures market by other means.
Where a unit commits the crime mentioned in the preceding paragraph, a fine shall be imposed on the unit, and the persons who are directly in charge and the other persons who are directly responsible for the crime shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.

Article 191 Whoever, for the purpose of concealing or disguising the source and nature of the proceeds and the gains derived from any drug-related crime, organized crime of a mafia nature, terrorist activities crime, smuggling crime, embezzlement or bribery crime, crime of disrupting the order of financial management, or financial fraud crime, commits any of the following acts, shall be subject to confiscation of the proceeds and gains derived from the above crimes, and shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if the circumstances are serious, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined:
(1) providing capital accounts;
(2) converting property into cash, financial instruments, or negotiable securities;
(3) transferring funds through transfer or other payment settlement methods;
(4) cross-border transfer of assets; or
(5) concealing or disguising the source and nature of criminal proceeds and their gains by other means.
Where a unit commits the crime mentioned in the preceding paragraph, a fine shall be imposed on the unit, and the persons who are directly in charge and the other persons who are directly responsible for the crime shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.

Article 193 Whoever, under any of the following circumstances, for the purpose of illegal possession, defrauds a bank or any other financial institution of a loan, if the amount is relatively large, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if the amount is huge or there are other serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan; if the amount is especially huge or there are other especially serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years or life imprisonment, and shall also be fined not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan or shall have his property confiscated:
(1) fabricating false reasons such as introducing foreign capital or projects;
(2) using false economic contracts;
(3) using false supporting documents;
(4) using false property right certificates as security or repeatedly providing security exceeding the value of the mortgaged property; or
(5) defrauding loans by other means.

Article 194 Whoever, under any of the following circumstances, engages in financial instrument fraud activities, if the amount is relatively large, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if the amount is huge or there are other serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan; if the amount is especially huge or there are other especially serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years or life imprisonment, and shall also be fined not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan or shall have his property confiscated:
(1) using forged or altered bills of exchange, promissory notes, or checks knowing them to be forged or altered;
(2) using invalidated bills of exchange, promissory notes, or checks knowing them to be invalid;
(3) fraudulently using another person's bills of exchange, promissory notes, or checks;
(4) issuing a rubber check or a check inconsistent with the reserved seal impression to defraud property; or
(5) the drawer of a bill of exchange or promissory note issues a bill of exchange or promissory note without a guaranteed source of funds or makes false entries at the time of issue to defraud property.
Whoever uses forged or altered other bank settlement vouchers, such as entrusted collection vouchers, remittance vouchers, or bank deposit certificates, shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.

Article 195 Whoever engages in any of the following activities of defrauding through letters of credit shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if the amount is huge or there are other serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan; if the amount is especially huge or there are other especially serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years or life imprisonment, and shall also be fined not less than 50,000 yuan but not more than 500,000 yuan or shall have his property confiscated:
(1) using forged or altered letters of credit or attached documents or instruments;
(2) using invalidated letters of credit;
(3) fraudulently obtaining letters of credit; or
(4) engaging in defrauding through letters of credit by other means.

Article 198 Whoever, under any of the following circumstances, engages in insurance fraud activities, if the amount is relatively large, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also be fined not less than 10,000 yuan but not more than 100,000 yuan; if the amount is huge or there are other serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan; if the amount is especially huge or there are other especially serious circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years, and shall also be fined not less than 20,000 yuan but not more than 200,000 yuan or shall have his property confiscated:
(1) the policyholder intentionally fabricates the subject matter of the insurance to defraud insurance money;
(2) the policyholder, the insured, or the beneficiary fabricates a false cause or exaggerates the extent of loss with respect to an insurance accident that has occurred to defraud insurance money;
(3) the policyholder, the insured, or the beneficiary fabricates an insurance accident that has never occurred to defraud insurance money;
(4) the policyholder or the insured intentionally causes an insurance accident involving property damage to defraud insurance money; or
(5) the policyholder or the beneficiary intentionally causes the death, disability, or illness of the insured to defraud insurance money.
Where any of the acts listed in subparagraphs (4) and (5) of the preceding paragraph also constitutes another crime, it shall be punished in accordance with the provisions on combined punishment for multiple crimes.
Where a unit commits the crime mentioned in the first paragraph, a fine shall be imposed on the unit, and the persons who are directly in charge and the other persons who are directly responsible for the crime shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention; if the amount is huge or there are other serious circumstances, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years; if the amount is especially huge or there are other especially serious circumstances, they shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years.
Where an expert evaluator, a witness, or a property assessor of an insurance accident intentionally provides false supporting documents to facilitate fraud by another person, he shall be deemed an accomplice to insurance fraud.

Article 217: Where a person, for purposes of profit, commits any of the following acts infringing copyright or rights related to copyright, if the amount of illegal gains is relatively large or if there are other serious circumstances, the person shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if the amount of illegal gains is huge or if there are other especially serious circumstances, the person shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years, and shall also be fined:

(1) without permission of the copyright owner, reproducing, distributing, or communicating to the public through information networks the owner's written works, music, works of fine art, audiovisual works, computer software, or other works as prescribed by laws and administrative regulations;

(2) publishing a book of which another person enjoys the exclusive right of publication;

(3) without permission of the producer of sound recordings or video recordings, reproducing, distributing, or communicating to the public through information networks the producer's sound recordings or video recordings;

(4) without permission of the performer, reproducing or distributing sound recordings or video recordings containing the performer's performance, or communicating the performer's performance to the public through information networks;

(5) producing or selling works of fine art bearing a forged signature of another person; or

(6) without permission of the copyright owner or owner of rights related to copyright, intentionally circumventing or destroying the technological measures adopted by the right owner to protect copyright or rights related to copyright in respect of the owner's works, sound recordings, video recordings, or the like.

Article 224: Whoever, under any of the following circumstances, with the intent of illegal possession, obtains property from the other party in the course of concluding or performing a contract, if the amount is relatively large, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention, and shall also, or shall only, be fined; if the amount is huge or there are other serious circumstances, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years and shall also be fined; if the amount is especially huge or there are other especially serious circumstances, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years or life imprisonment, and shall also be fined or have property confiscated:
(1) concluding a contract in the name of a fictitious unit or by impersonating another person;
(2) providing a guarantee by using forged, altered, or invalidated negotiable instruments or other false documents of title;
(3) without actual performance capability, by means of first performing a small part of the contract or part of the contract, inducing the other party to continue to conclude and perform the contract;
(4) after receiving the goods, payment, advance payment, or guaranteed property delivered by the other party, absconding; or
(5) obtaining the property of the other party by other means.
Article 224a: Whoever organizes or leads pyramid selling activities which, under the guise of promoting commodities, providing services, or other business operations, require participants to obtain membership by paying fees or purchasing commodities or services, and form hierarchies in a certain order, directly or indirectly using the number of recruited persons as the basis for remuneration or rebate, inducing or coercing participants to continue recruiting others to join, obtaining property, and disrupting the economic and social order, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention and shall also be fined; where the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years and shall also be fined.

Article 225: Whoever, in violation of state regulations, commits any of the following illegal business operations, disrupting market order, where the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention, and shall also, or shall only, be fined not less than one time but not more than five times the illegal gains; where the circumstances are especially serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years, and shall also be fined not less than one time but not more than five times the illegal gains or have property confiscated:
(1) engaging in the business of goods that are exclusively for business or sale by designated entities as provided by laws or administrative regulations, or other goods whose trading is restricted, without permission;
(2) buying or selling import or export licenses, certificates of origin for import or export, or other business licenses or approval documents provided by laws or administrative regulations;
(3) illegally engaging in securities, futures, or insurance businesses, or illegally engaging in fund payment settlement business, without the approval of the relevant competent authority of the state; or
(4) other illegal business operations that seriously disrupt market order.

Article 226: Whoever, by means of violence or threats, commits any of the following acts, where the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention, and shall also, or shall only, be fined; where the circumstances are especially serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years and shall also be fined:
(1) forcing others to buy or sell commodities;
(2) forcing others to provide or accept services;
(3) forcing others to participate in or withdraw from a bid or auction;
(4) forcing others to transfer or acquire shares, bonds, or other assets of a company or enterprise; or
(5) forcing others to participate in or withdraw from specific business activities.

Article 236: Whoever rapes a woman by violence, coercion, or other means shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years.
Whoever has sexual intercourse with a girl under the age of 14 shall be deemed to have committed rape and shall be given a severe punishment.
Whoever rapes a woman or has sexual intercourse with a girl under the age of 14 under any of the following circumstances shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years, life imprisonment, or death:
(1) the circumstances of the rape or sexual intercourse are odious;
(2) the offender has raped multiple women or has had sexual intercourse with multiple girls under the age of 14;
(3) the offender rapes a woman or has sexual intercourse with a girl under the age of 14 in a public place in a brazen manner;
(4) the offender commits gang rape;
(5) the offender has sexual intercourse with a girl under the age of 10 or causes harm to the girl; or
(6) the offender causes serious bodily injury, death, or other serious consequences to the victim.
Article 236a: Where a person who has special duties such as guardianship, adoption, care, education, or medical treatment towards a female minor over the age of 14 but under the age of 16 engages in sexual relations with that female minor, the offender shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years; where the circumstances are odious, the offender shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years.
Where, in addition to the act mentioned in the preceding paragraph, the act also constitutes a crime under Article 236 of this Law, the conviction and punishment shall be imposed in accordance with the provisions for the heavier punishment.

Article 240: Whoever abducts and traffics in women or children shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years and shall also be fined; under any of the following circumstances, the offender shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years or life imprisonment, and shall also be fined or have property confiscated; where the circumstances are especially serious, the offender shall be sentenced to death and shall also have property confiscated:
(1) the ringleader of a group that abducts and traffics in women or children;
(2) the offender abducts and traffics in three or more women or children;
(3) the offender rapes an abducted woman;
(4) the offender induces or forces an abducted woman to engage in prostitution, or sells an abducted woman to another person who forces her to engage in prostitution;
(5) the offender kidnaps a woman or child by violence, coercion, or anesthesia for the purpose of selling the victim;
(6) the offender steals an infant or a child for the purpose of selling the victim;
(7) the offender causes serious bodily injury, death, or other serious consequences to an abducted woman or child or their relatives; or
(8) the offender sells a woman or child outside the country.
Abducting and trafficking in women or children means, for the purpose of selling, committing any of the acts of abducting, kidnapping, buying, selling, escorting, or transiting women or children.

Article 243 Whoever, by violence, coercion or other means, forcibly takes public or private property shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years and shall also be fined; whoever falls under any of the following circumstances shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years, life imprisonment or death and shall also be fined or have his or her property confiscated:
(1) forcibly entering a residence for robbery;
(2) committing robbery on a public means of transport;
(3) robbing a bank or any other financial institution;
(4) committing robbery repeatedly or robbing a huge amount of property;
(5) causing serious injury or death to another person during robbery;
(6) impersonating a member of the armed forces or a police officer to commit robbery;
(7) committing robbery with a gun;
(8) robbing military supplies or materials allocated for emergency relief, disaster relief or social assistance.

Article 292: Where a crowd gathered to engage in affray, the principal offenders and other active participants shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, criminal detention, or public surveillance; under any of the following circumstances, the principal offenders and other active participants shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years:
(1) repeatedly gathering a crowd to engage in affray;
(2) where the number of participants in the affray is large, the scale is large, and the social impact is adverse;
(3) gathering a crowd to engage in affray in public places or on major traffic routes, causing serious chaos in social order; or
(4) gathering a crowd to engage in affray with weapons.
Where a crowd gathered to engage in affray causes serious injury or death to any person, the offenders shall be convicted and punished in accordance with Articles 234 and 232 of this Law.

Article 293: Whoever commits any of the following acts of picking quarrels and provoking trouble, thereby undermining social order, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years, criminal detention, or public surveillance:
(1) beating another person at will, where the circumstances are flagrant;
(2) pursuing, intercepting, verbally abusing, or intimidating another person, where the circumstances are flagrant;
(3) forcibly taking or demanding, or arbitrarily destroying or occupying public or private property, where the circumstances are serious; or
(4) causing a disturbance in a public place, resulting in serious disorder in the public place.
Whoever gathers others to repeatedly commit the acts in the preceding paragraph, thereby seriously undermining social order, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five but not more than ten years, and may also be fined.
Article 293(A): Whoever, under any of the following circumstances, collects illegal debts generated by high-interest lending, where the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, criminal detention, or public surveillance, and/or a fine:
(1) using violence or coercion;
(2) restricting another person's personal freedom or intruding into another person's residence; or
(3) intimidating, stalking, or harassing another person.

Article 309: Whoever commits any of the following acts disrupting the order of a court shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, criminal detention, public surveillance, or a fine:
(1) Assembling a crowd to make a din or storm a court;
(2) Assaulting a judicial officer or a participant in a proceeding;
(3) Insulting, defaming, or threatening a judicial officer or a participant in a proceeding, disobeying the court's order to stop, and seriously disrupting the order of the court; or
(4) Damaging court facilities, seizing or damaging litigation documents or evidence, or otherwise disrupting the order of the court, if the circumstances are serious.

Article 315: Any criminal lawfully detained who commits any of the following acts disrupting the order of custody, if the circumstances are serious, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years:
(1) Assaulting custodial personnel;
(2) Organizing other detainees to disrupt the order of custody;
(3) Assembling a crowd to engage in disturbances to disrupt the normal order of custody; or
(4) Assaulting, physically punishing, or instigating another person to assault or physically punish other detainees.

Article 318: Whoever organizes another person to illegally cross the national border (or frontier) shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than two years but not more than seven years, and shall also be fined; in any of the following circumstances, the person shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than seven years or life imprisonment, and shall also be fined or be subject to confiscation of property:
(1) Being a ringleader of a group that organizes others to illegally cross the national border (or frontier);
(2) Repeatedly organizing others to illegally cross the national border (or frontier) or organizing a large number of persons to do so;
(3) Causing serious injury or death to the organized persons;
(4) Depriving or restricting the personal freedom of the organized persons;
(5) Using violence or threats to resist inspection;
(6) The illegal gains are huge; or
(7) Having other especially serious circumstances.
Where a person commits the crime in the preceding paragraph and also commits acts of killing, injuring, raping, trafficking, or other crimes against the organized persons, or acts of killing or injuring inspection personnel, the person shall be punished in accordance with the provisions on combined punishment for multiple crimes.

Article 321 Whoever transports another person to illegally cross the national border (border) shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years, criminal detention or public surveillance, and shall be fined; if the circumstances fall under any of the following, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years, and shall be fined:
(1) repeatedly committing the act of transportation or transporting a large number of persons;
(2) the vessels, vehicles or other means of transportation used do not possess the necessary safety conditions, which is sufficient to cause serious consequences;
(3) the amount of illegal gains is huge;
(4) there are other especially serious circumstances.
If, in the course of transporting another person to illegally cross the national border (border), he causes serious injury or death to the person being transported, or resists inspection by violence or threat, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than seven years, and shall be fined.
If, while committing the crime as set forth in the preceding two paragraphs, he also commits criminal acts such as killing, injuring, raping, or trafficking the person being transported, or killing or injuring an inspector, he shall be punished in accordance with the provisions on combined punishment for several crimes.

Article 328 Whoever robs and excavates an ancient cultural site or ancient tomb of historical, artistic or scientific value shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than ten years, and shall be fined; if the circumstances are relatively minor, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years, criminal detention or public surveillance, and shall be fined; if the circumstances fall under any of the following, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than ten years or life imprisonment, and shall be fined or have his property confiscated:
(1) robbing and excavating an ancient cultural site or ancient tomb that is determined to be a major cultural relic site under State protection or a provincial-level cultural relic site;
(2) being a ringleader of a group that robs and excavates ancient cultural sites or ancient tombs;
(3) repeatedly robbing and excavating ancient cultural sites or ancient tombs;
(4) robbing and excavating an ancient cultural site or ancient tomb, and stealing valuable cultural relics or causing serious damage to valuable cultural relics.
Whoever robs and excavates fossils of ancient humans or ancient vertebrates of scientific value under State protection shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.

Article 330 Whoever, in violation of the Law on Prevention and Treatment of Infectious Diseases, falls under any of the following circumstances, causing the spread of a Class A infectious disease and a infectious disease for which prevention and control measures as determined according to law are adopted, or causing a serious risk of spread thereof, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention; if the consequences are especially serious, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years:
(1) the drinking water supplied by a water supply unit fails to meet the hygiene standards prescribed by the State;
(2) refusing to disinfect sewage, waste, premises or articles contaminated by the pathogens of infectious diseases in accordance with the hygiene requirements raised by the disease prevention and control institution;
(3) permitting or conniving at a patient of an infectious disease, a pathogen carrier or a suspected patient of an infectious disease to engage in any work that is prohibited by the health administration department under the State Council to be engaged in by such persons and that is likely to cause the spread of the infectious disease;
(4) selling or transporting articles that are contaminated or may be contaminated by the pathogens of an infectious disease in an epidemic area and failing to disinfect them; or
(5) refusing to carry out the prevention and control measures proposed, in accordance with the Law on Prevention and Treatment of Infectious Diseases, by the people's government at or above the county level or the disease prevention and control institution.
If a unit commits the crime as set forth in the preceding paragraph, it shall be fined, and the persons who are directly in charge and the other persons who are directly liable for the crime shall be punished in accordance with the provisions of the preceding paragraph.
The scope of Class A infectious diseases shall be determined in accordance with the Law of the People's Republic of China on Prevention and Treatment of Infectious Diseases and the relevant regulations of the State Council.

Article 338 Whoever, in violation of the State regulations, discharges, dumps or disposes of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases, toxic substances or other harmful substances, thereby seriously polluting the environment, shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention, and shall also be fined or only be fined; if the circumstances are serious, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than three years but not more than seven years, and shall be fined; if the circumstances fall under any of the following, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than seven years, and shall be fined:
(1) discharging, dumping or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases or toxic substances in such key protected areas as drinking water source protection zones and core protected areas of nature reserves determined according to law, where the circumstances are especially serious;
(2) discharging, dumping or disposing of radioactive waste, waste containing pathogens of infectious diseases or toxic substances into the waters of important rivers or lakes designated by the State, where the circumstances are especially serious;
(3) causing the basic functions of large quantities of permanent basic farmland to be lost or permanently damaged; or
(4) causing multiple persons to suffer serious injury or serious illness, or causing a person to suffer severe disability or death.
If the act as set forth in the preceding paragraph also constitutes another crime, the offender shall be convicted and punished in accordance with the provisions on the heavier punishment.

Article 408 Where a state functionary responsible for environmental protection supervision and administration is grossly irresponsible, resulting in a major environmental pollution accident, causing significant losses to public or private property, or serious consequences of personal injury or death, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than three years or criminal detention.
Article 408-1 Where a state functionary responsible for food and drug safety supervision and administration abuses his power or neglects his duty, falls under any of the following circumstances, and causes serious consequences or has other severe circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not more than five years or criminal detention; where especially serious consequences are caused or there are other especially severe circumstances, he shall be sentenced to fixed-term imprisonment of not less than five years but not more than ten years:
(1) concealing or falsely reporting food safety accidents or drug safety incidents;
(2) failing to investigate and punish serious food and drug safety violations as legally required;
(3) granting permission to applications that do not meet the conditions during the approval and evaluation of drugs and special foods;
(4) failing to transfer matters that shall be transferred according to law to the judicial authorities for investigation of criminal liability;
(5) having other acts of abusing power or neglecting duty.
Where a person engages in malpractices for personal gain and commits the crime in the preceding paragraph, he shall be given a severe punishment.
